syntax:

upper_bound(f, l, val);
upper_bound(f, l, val, comp);

f: iterator to beginning of sequence
l: iterator to end of sequence
val: value whose upper bound needed to be found
comp: -- not clear yet --

What it returns ?

(** It alwsys works in sorted sequence)
It returns the index of the first element which is not less than the
given value;

example:

a = [10, 20, 30, 30, 35, 40];
lower_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), 35);

OUTPUT: 4

upper_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), 35);
OUTPUT: 5

